1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:05,764
Testing one, two, three. I'm saying a few words right now.

2
00:00:06,264 --> 00:00:09,737
Testing one, two, three. I'm saying a few words right now.

3
00:00:10,570 --> 00:00:14,785
Okay, yes, that was obvious. The first was the original recording.

4
00:00:14,785 --> 00:00:18,233
The second was generated locally from a fifteen-second sample.

5
00:00:18,233 --> 00:00:19,766
The cool part is,

6
00:00:19,766 --> 00:00:23,597
the generated audio was done on a six-year-old MacBook Pro,

7
00:00:23,597 --> 00:00:25,130
using Mynah with chatterbox.

8
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:27,260
As a matter of fact,

9
00:00:27,260 --> 00:00:31,368
this entire video has been narrated using Mynah on the same 2020 M1

10
00:00:31,368 --> 00:00:32,000
MacBook Pro.

11
00:00:32,550 --> 00:00:34,571
So, here's how it works.

12
00:00:34,571 --> 00:00:38,614
Start by recording or uploading five seconds of clean speech.

13
00:00:38,614 --> 00:00:41,444
Mynah compiles the voice once using chatterbox,

14
00:00:41,444 --> 00:00:43,870
then reuses it for every line.

15
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:48,280
Paste in a script. Blank lines become separate, editable takes.

16
00:00:48,850 --> 00:00:52,450
Generate each line independently, and Mynah caches the result.

17
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,800
Preview the complete mix directly in your browser.

18
00:00:56,150 --> 00:00:58,050
This runs entirely on your own machine.

19
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:01,380
No account, no API key, and nothing is uploaded.

20
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:07,340
If one line sounds wrong, change it and re-roll only that line.

21
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:08,920
The rest stays untouched.

22
00:01:09,290 --> 00:01:11,190
This runs entirely on your own machine.

23
00:01:11,680 --> 00:01:15,650
No account, no API key, and not one byte leaves the room.

24
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:19,940
No cloud API. The project is open source on GitHub.
